' M-ROKU-06 (review roku__crossfe M6): design-plane law — the WHOLE channel is
' laid out on a hardcoded 1280x720 plane (112 XML width/height/loadWidth/
' loadHeight attribute pins across 37 files at cce1b34; PlayerScene.brs sizes
' the Video node
' 1280x720 at :1185 and :3000; there is zero coordinate scaling anywhere —
' no resolutionRatio, viewBounds, GetVisibleRect or root Group scale, and
' videoMode is read only for the About screen). With 'full' declared beside
' 'hd', RokuOS runs 1080p devices NATIVELY at 1920x1080 and the 720p layout
' sits unscaled in the top-left two-thirds of the screen. Declaring 'hd'
' alone makes the OS render the 1280x720 canvas and upscale it — the standard
' fixed-layout posture. 'sd' is intentionally absent: the app is https-only
' modern and a 1280-wide plane never fits a 640x480 screen. Re-declare 'full'
' only TOGETHER with a real resolution-aware layout; CHECK38 pins the
' declaration, the plane's FHD-only outliers and this comment's presence.
ui_resolutions=hd

rsg_version=7.0

screensaver_title=Phlix
screensaver_private=false

